Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:45:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 42/68] urltest: the Clash API's delay test does not wait for
 nested selections

The Clash API's delay test of a group returns once the members are tested,
without the group's selection, which may run download tests of up to 15 s per
candidate ("the Clash API's round does not wait"). A nested urltest group
among the members still selected inside the batch: the delay test of a
selector holding urltest groups, as podkop's dashboard runs with a 10 s
timeout, or of a urltest group of groups, waited for every nested download
test, and its timeout canceled the tests of the other members.

URLTestOutbounds and the round take wait: the periodic round of a group and
the daemon keep waiting for nested selections, since the group above selects
by the nested group's new choice; the Clash API does not, and the nested
group selects afterwards, as its own delay test already did.
